<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Admin · authum</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<% @include('styles') %>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="topnav">
    <div class="brand">authum</div>
    <a href="/logout">Log out</a>
  </div>
  <h1>Admin</h1>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="lede">Traefik calls <code>/auth/verify</code> on each protected request. Unknown hosts are denied. Allowed requests get the identity headers named in Sites. After form login, users hit <code>https://{host}/_authum/login</code> once so each site gets its own cookie (same session id).</p>

    <h2>ACL</h2>
    <p class="lede">First matching row wins; no match means deny.</p>
    <ul class="help">
      <li><code>user</code>: anyone, a user, or a group (<code>*</code>, <code>#id</code>, <code>@id</code>). Renames do not break rules.</li>
      <li><code>site</code>: any site or one Sites row (numeric id or <code>*</code>).</li>
      <li><code>path</code>: RE2-style regex against the request path (e.g. <code>^/</code>, <code>(?i)\.pdf$</code>).</li>
      <li><code>method</code>: <code>*</code>, one method, or a comma-separated list (e.g. <code>GET,OPTIONS,PROPFIND</code>).</li>
    </ul>
    <%= safe @acl_table %>

    <h2>Sites</h2>
    <p class="lede">Numeric <code>id</code> is what ACL rows and login redirects use. <code>name</code> is a renameable label. Host has no scheme. Configure Traefik <code>authResponseHeaders</code> for the header names.</p>
    <%= safe @sites_table %>

    <h2>Users</h2>
    <p class="lede">Usernames are <code>[A-Za-z0-9_]</code> only and cannot be only digits. The env admin user cannot be renamed, deleted, or disabled; its password is reset from <code>AUTHUM_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> on every startup. Discord sign-ups start <strong>disabled</strong> until you enable them here. Set Discord ID to link an account to a Discord snowflake (clear to unlink).</p>
    <%= safe @users_html %>

    <h2>Groups</h2>
    <p class="lede">Group names use the same rules as usernames (<code>[A-Za-z0-9_]</code>, not only digits). Put people in a group, then use <code>@id</code> in the ACL (group numeric id). Renaming a group does not break ACL rules. Deleting a group removes its ACL rules via foreign key cascade.</p>
    <%= safe @groups_html %>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
